                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237207971",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197970520745",
                            "num_reviews": 122,
                            "playtime_forever": 191,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 138,
                            "last_played": 1792053902
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This has become my favorite game series since Talos Principle without all the heavy AI philosophy. While this game focuses mainly on color mixing, the soundtrack is perfect for getting into that end-of-the-day mindset where you can let your thoughts and problem solving skills automate themselves in your head and reach a different state of mind. I find myself stumped, as often can happen with puzzle games, but stumped in a way that I'm okay with. Once I finally solve one, often it's the case that I haven't even 100% had a plan before managing to get it right. This makes the survey of the completed puzzle afterword a learning experience, and leaves me with an admiration of the cleverness and sometimes even beauty of the puzzle design.\n\nIf you're into Talos, I highly recommend you give this a try. As a bonus, I'd recommend picking up the bundle of all the games; there's also an \"Evolved\" series of this same game as well for even more puzzles. Just wonderful so far IMHO.",
